  "notes": "{婚約|こんやく} is a formal agreement to marry. It can be used as a noun or with する as a suru verb.\n\nWORD FORMATION:\n{婚|こん} (marriage) + {約|やく} (promise, agreement)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {婚約|こんやく}する: to get engaged\n- {婚約|こんやく}を{解消|かいしょう}する: to break off an engagement\n- {婚約|こんやく}{指輪|ゆびわ}: engagement ring\n- {婚約|こんやく}{発表|はっぴょう}: engagement announcement\n- {婚約|こんやく}{者|しゃ}: fiancé/fiancée\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nIn Japan, {婚約|こんやく} may be formalized through {結納|ゆいのう} (a traditional betrothal ceremony involving gift exchange between families), though this practice is becoming less common in modern times.\n\nRELATED:\n- {結婚|けっこん}: marriage\n- {結納|ゆいのう}: betrothal ceremony",
